<title>UK: Commercial Union off amid weak gilt market.</title>
<headline>Commercial Union off amid weak gilt market.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Commercial Union Plc led most UK insurance shares lower amid growing concern about higher gilt yields, dealers said.</p>
<p>At 1223 GMT, Commercial Union shares were off 19p, or 2.75 percent, to 672-1/2p.</p>
<p>Elsewhere, shares in General Accident Plc lost 21-1/2p to 800-1/2p, a six-week low, while shares in Royal &amp; Sun Alliance Insurance Group Plc tumbled 10-1/2p to 450-1/2p.</p>
</text>
